<title>GERMANY: Pan-German June numbers in work flat in June.</title>
<headline>Pan-German June numbers in work flat in June.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN NUMBERS IN WORK	   Jun 96     May 96     Jun 95</p>
<p> Number in work (1)(unadj, million)    34.511     34.426     34.815</p>
<p> Number in work (1)(seas adj, million) 34.533     34.535     34.838</p>
<p> Number in work (2)(seas adj, million) 34.576     34.577     34.878</p>
<p>WEST GERMAN</p>
<p> Number in work (unadj,million)	  28.252     28.183     28.499</p>
<p> Number in work (seas adj, million)    28.243     28.248     28.490</p>
<p>EAST GERMAN</p>
<p> Number in work (unadj, million)	  6.322	6.297	6.376</p>
<p> Number in work (seas adj, million)     6.333	6.329	6.388</p>
<p>NOTE - Pan-German figure marked (1) refer to people living in Germany. Those marked (2), as well as all the west and east German figures, refer to people working in the respective regions but not necessarily living in Germany.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
